es and scripts.\\n   - If issues remain, tag ONLY the responsible author (`@env`, `@anim`, or `@sfx`). When everything passes, post a concise verification summary tagging `@coordinator`.\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:25:52\",\"kind\":\"brief\",\"request_id\":\"fd4184d2-55ba-4325-9d40-4a9cdf02fcfa\"},{\"seq\":2,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@env You are the Environment, Materials \\u0026 Lighting Author (`env`) for `D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar` (Blender 5.3.0 at `D:\\\\APPs\\\\steam\\\\steamapps\\\\common\\\\Blender\\\\blender.exe`, pure CPU EEVEE).\\n\\nOWNERSHIP \\u0026 STRICT BOUNDARIES:\\n- You OWN: `pipeline/v5_env.py`, `textures/*` (and `pipeline/gen_textures.py` if you add a reusable texture generator), `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend`, and `renders_v5/preview/*`.\\n- DO NOT TOUCH: `pipeline/v5_anim.py`, `pipeline/v5_clay.py`, `pipeline/v5_stills.py`, `pipeline/v5_viewport_fast.py`, `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend`, `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `renders_v5/clay_frames/`, `pipeline/mux_*.sh`, or `.md`/`.txt` docs.\\n- Mention discipline: `@name` wakes that agent. Do not CC. Hand off to `@anim` when `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` is finalized; tag `@coordinator` only if blocked.\\n\\nMISSION — Upgrade V5 Track Environment, Car Materials \\u0026 Golden-Hour Lighting:\\n1) Read `pipeline/v5_env.py` and `docs/README_V5.md` (especially §9 pitfalls: road specular \\u003c= 0.03 to avoid white sun wedge, `light_linking.receiver_collection` on car fill lights so no bright square hits asphalt, decal brightness balance, CPU budget ~2.3s/frame).\\n2) Check `read_board` for `@verifier`'s Round 1 audit findings before finalizing (you can inspect `v5_env.py` and prototype immediately while `@verifier` runs).\\n3) Implement high-impact improvements in `pipeline/v5_env.py` (and `textures/`):\\n   - Outliner \\u0026 Scene Cleanliness: Ensure ALL assembly Empty parents (`EM_*`) are placed in their matching `V5_04_Stands` / `V5_05_Pit` / `V5_06_Props` collections (none stranded in root `Scene Collection`!), purge unused orphan meshes/materials at save time, and keep total object count lean (\\u003c1,050 objects) so CPU render speed stays fast.\\n   - Track Surface \\u0026 Corner Realism: Add heavy-braking rubber skidmark/darkening zones on the racing line approaching major braking corners (Village/Loop, Brooklands/Luffield, Stowe, Vale/Club) + subtle off-line rubber marbles/dust variation (`Specular IOR Level` strictly \\u003c= 0.03 on all road/line/kerb shaders!). Add DRS zone marker boards (`DRS`) before Hangar Straight \\u0026 Wellington Straight, and apex bollards / inner sausage kerbs at chicanes/slow corners without intruding onto `racing_xy`!\\n   - Pit Lane \\u0026 Trackside Polish: Refine `textures/` (`pit_garage.png`, `ad_boards.png`, `bigscreen.png`) for crisp broadcast-grade F1 graphic fidelity; add pit-wall timing gantry / pit exit light post (`GREEN` LED) on pit wall.\\n   - Sky Dome \\u0026 Dusk Lighting: Upgrade `V5_SkyDome` from coarse 7-step vertex banding to smooth continuous multi-band horizon gradient + subtle warm solar azimuth glow aligned with sun direction so low-angle shots have zero polygon/color banding in the sky! Keep shadows crisp and car highlight wrap clean.\\n   - Car Material \\u0026 Brake Rotor Readiness: Inspect car meshes imported from `pipeline/v4_stage_rig.blend` — refine body paint clearcoat/metallic sheen, carbon fiber weave roughness contrast on wings/floor/halo, tire sidewall vs tread rubber contrast, and ensure brake rotor/caliper or brake-glow material exists with a clean named emission input (e.g. `MAT_BrakeGlow` or named node) if helpful for `@anim` to keyframe `brake_heat` glow (document exact material/node name in your post to `@anim`!).\\n4) Run `\\\"D:\\\\APPs\\\\steam\\\\steamapps\\\\common\\\\Blender\\\\blender.exe\\\" -b -P pipeline/v5_env.py` and `pipeline/v5_preview.py` (or a quick preview script writing to `renders_v5/preview/`), inspect the rendered preview JPGs with `read_file